WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Our next guest is

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.068 size:81% position:41% line:92%
a Tony-nominated actor

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.336 line:92%
who you know, from movies like

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Inside Out";

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:04.938 line:92%
and shows like "Big Mouth,

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Spin City,"
and "Documentary Now!"

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:09.476
You can catch him on season
of "Everything's Gonna Be Okay,"

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
which airs Thursdays
on Freeform.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:14.280
New episodes are available
the following day on Hulu.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.215 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hello. Hi, there!
-Well, look at you.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-You're as tall as can be.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-I hope you don't mind us

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.189 size:78% position:39% line:92%
settling in out here.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I don't mind,
but I don't like it.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, my guests stuck
in their car?

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
How drab!
-We're absolutely fine.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We've got CDs.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.831 line:92%
-I mean, even with CDs...

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
There must simply be
more to life

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.869 line:92%
than this driveway to nowhere.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:36.436 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, we're fine.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
Plus, nobody's really trying
to live their lives,

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
nowadays, are they?
-Uh...

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
our very good friend
Richard Kind.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:45.945 size:78% position:39% line:92%
How are you, Richard?

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, Seth, I didn't know you -
Oh.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
-I'm so upset

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:53.653
I'm not in-studio because
need a fourth of these.

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.056 size:84% position:42%
-You do get a free mug
every time you're here,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we refuse to give it
for people

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
who don't have the courage
to come to the studio.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:00.927 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.430 size:78% position:39%
-I'm doing very well.
How are you doing?

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm doing great.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.099 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You've been very busy.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've kept busy
during this year

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
where a lot of people haven't.
-I got to tell you,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.138 line:92%
since July, just working.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
I, you know, grew a beard
to play a scientist

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's living
out in the wilderness --

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:23.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
not a comedy -- who's got
military secrets for aliens.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had this beard and I go,
"Well, why not?"

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so the part
didn't call for it,

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:31.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you know me,
I just meet the thing halfwa

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-and I'll, "Hey,
it's got a beard!

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:36.196 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, okay. Why not?"

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:39.566
-Is there anyone you were
aiming for with the beard?

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there anybody
you were trying to emulate

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.902 line:92%
Because it's very unique.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:46.840
-I am the president of the
Mandy Patinkin Fan Club.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
No.
It grows in like this!

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.178 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I will tell you this.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
Believe it or not,
I tried to dye it one time

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
dye the hair.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:02.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And have you seen old ladie
with blue in their hair?

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.990 size:75% position:38% line:92%
That's what happens.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I didn't know
and I didn't do it --

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go get one
of those things and go,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:08.561 line:92%
"Oh, no, no, no, no, no!"

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.931
And I just washed it
very quickly and it didn't take.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.266 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But it grows in weird.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.268 line:92%
It's like Hemingway, you know?

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like the idea
of you playing a scientist

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has military secrets
about aliens.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.643 size:84% position:42%
Is Richard Kind someone
who believes in aliens?

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. No.
-Okay.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do not,
although I got to tell you

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.349 size:88% position:44% line:92%
the guy who directed it,

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
his name is Thomas DeLonge
Tom DeLonge.

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:35.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was a singer for Blink-182.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He loves aliens!

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He loves UFOs.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.693 line:92%
Has met with the Pentagon.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the whole time
we're shooting --

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.063 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and he's a lovely guy

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:47.901 size:78% position:39%
and a good director,
everything like that.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.701 line:92%
He was a great skateboarde

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.671
and he's a rock 'n' roller
who's a director now, okay

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-So I'm like memorizing lines.

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.241 line:92%
I'm not going to get into parts,

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you know how --
Okay, but I'm memorizing.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.378
I'm in the scene and everything.
He goes --

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:01.080 size:84% position:42%
[ California accent ]
No, no, no, dude, dude!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.415 line:92%
You got to listen to this story.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:03.883 line:92%
There was one time this alien --

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.519 line:92%
I'm going, "Tom! Tom! Direct

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't tell me your stories
about aliens.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me -- I'm working, here!
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:14.060
And, you know, in between shots,
so, yeah, it was fun.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was hilarious,
doing this thing.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.832
You never know whether or no
a movie's going to be seen

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's called
"Monsters of California."

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.771
I don't know. It's about,
you know, with young kids

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:28.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm the old guy
who has military secrets.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:29.242 size:75% position:38% line:92%
So that's what I do.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:33.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What about ghosts?
Do you believe in ghosts?

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:35.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I used to not.
-Okay.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how these stories
always start.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.419 size:75% position:38%
-No, no, no, no, no.
And I used to not,

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:40.820 line:92%
so, therefore, I'm a convert

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.855 line:92%
At Second City, one time -

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:43.856 line:92%
Did you work at Second City?

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I never did, no.
-Did your brother?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did Josh work there,
your brother?
-No.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.061 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-No. Okay.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I've been there.
I've been there plenty, yeah

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:52.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, but the one
in Santa Monica

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:56.736
and, one night, literally,
we're going out for a scene.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was with Robin Duke --
which tells you how long ago -

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.274 line:92%
and we're holding two chairs

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, all of a sudden,
I feel a chair getting pulle

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.644 line:92%
and I go, "Robin, Robin, stop!

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's on the other sid
of the stage.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I could feel myself
getting pulled.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.884 line:92%
And we go out and we asked -

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:17.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
One night, there was no wa
to get backstage, okay?

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.959
And we're working. We're doing
improv, everything like that

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:23.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
We come backstage.
There are chairs on the couch.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:27.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
All the tapes from previousl
recorded improvs

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.469 line:92%
were scattered on the floor.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.671 line:92%
And you can't get back there

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.106 size:84% position:42% line:92%
So, what? I don't know.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.775 line:92%
And so, do I believe in ghosts

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But no.

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't. I don't.
-So you think a ghost hate

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fact that you recorded
improv shows?

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were like,
"These are not --

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
They're only good
in the moment."

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:49.322
-They're only good in the moment
or for ghosts to knock over.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.291 size:78% position:39%
That's all they are.
They're fodder for --

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:52.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes.
Two, we're left on

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they liked that
particular night of improv

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:57.997
They said, "These are okay
The rest, they're garbage!

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.365 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Get them out of here!"

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did not realize we both wen
to Northwestern University

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not realize one of you
daughters is going there.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of my daughters,
my oldest daughter, Skye,

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:11.411
is going to Northwestern,
but she's going by Zoom.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.545 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She's in North Carolina.

00:05:12.545 --> 00:05:14.447 line:92%
I feel very bad for these kids

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
In essence, she's going
for, you know,

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.385 line:92%
DeVry Institute for $75,000.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But, you know, she's going

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:25.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very tragic, with the kid
and their learning.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:26.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't like this.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.795
-Well, I went and, again,
I'd very much like being

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
with you in person
and I miss being around people

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:37.537
I know you sort of filled ou
your house over this pandemic.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:38.771 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You guys got a dog.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:40.406 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How's dog life?

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.642 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-We have a dog.

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.177 size:75% position:38% line:92%
The dog is adorable.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a puppy.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My advice is get a puppy
at two years of age.

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:49.449 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I had a friend who said,

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Old people should be shot
at birth,"

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel the same way
about puppies.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:57.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
Puppies should be born
at two years old.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.425 line:92%
The dog's name is Wilson.

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to change the name
to Mistake.

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:05.264 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.499 line:92%
-Our apartment is a toilet

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
The cleanest place
in the apartment

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:09.702 size:88% position:44% line:92%
is our kitty litter box.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:12.672 line:92%
We have two cats and a ferret.

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:13.973 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I hate the ferret.

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:16.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love all the animals,
but, no.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:20.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know that, in New York
ferrets are illegal?

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.148 size:78% position:39%
-I did not know that.
-So I'm a scofflaw

00:06:22.148 --> 00:06:23.783 line:92%
and I'm and on national tele--

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.017 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I hate this ferret.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
They say,
"Oh, well, it has a musk."

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.187 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It doesn't have a musk.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:29.188 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It stinks.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It just smells.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:34.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're adorable-looking
and they move like this.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:35.928 line:92%
They're funny, like dolphins

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:36.996 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hate ferrets.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.231 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Love my puppy.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.165 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hate my puppy.

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:40.166 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's just, you know,

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:42.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
puppies are babies born
without diapers.

00:06:42.602 --> 00:06:46.339
That's what they are.
-Who talked you into the ferret?

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My daughter,
my youngest daughter.

00:06:48.808 --> 00:06:50.243 line:92%
There was a ferret in her class.

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.578 line:92%
She says, "I want a ferret."

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You have a child.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is it like to say no
to your child?

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:57.850 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's really hard.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't feel like
they're quite old enough

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.686 line:92%
to like have strong desires.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:02.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
But would you describe yoursel
as a pushover?

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I am the pushover
of the two parents.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:10.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am. Well, I have to admit,
this dog, the puppy,

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:12.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
was purchased
while I was in L.A.,

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they wanted
to "surprise" me with it.

00:07:14.867 --> 00:07:17.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Okay? And I get this text

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.772 line:92%
from the veterinarian, saying,

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The new dog has an appointmen
this Wednesday at 9:30.

00:07:25.178 --> 00:07:29.182
'Y' for yes, 'N' for no,"
and I'm going, "What?"

00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:32.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I call up and I go,
"Do we have a puppy?"

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:34.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they go,
"Oh, it was a surprise."

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:36.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-No! No! Talk to me.

00:07:36.556 --> 00:07:39.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm the only logical one
in the family.

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:40.359 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Talk to me, first.

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:43.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a horror!
It's a horror!

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:45.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
It's just awful!

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's adorable
and it's so smart.

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:53.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's "Marley &amp; Me"
and I don't know what to do.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:54.407 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's another baby.

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:55.942 line:92%
It's a baby without diapers.

00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:57.577 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It just poops.

00:07:57.577 --> 00:07:58.244 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Although, so smart,

00:07:58.244 --> 00:08:00.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Snapping fingers ] the minut
it came in the house,

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.583 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
onto the pad.

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it doesn't know how to pee
outside or poop outside.

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have to teach a dog to pee
and poop outside.

00:08:11.691 --> 00:08:12.692 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Who would've thought?

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:15.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
In New York.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:16.562 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Who would've thought?

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.064 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I mean, I don't know.

00:08:18.064 --> 00:08:20.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a wreck.
I'm a wreck.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're going to get
through this.

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:24.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-I want to ask you this.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-COVID's a snap.
Puppies, that's --

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Oh, my gosh! Yes, what?

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:33.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lot of people --
You know, you have a very --

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:34.714 line:92%
A lot of people know your voice.

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:36.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very
distinguishable voice

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:40.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-and I have heard
that you have advice.

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not an impressionist,
per se,

00:08:42.288 --> 00:08:44.590 line:92%
but you have a way for peopl

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get into a Richard Kind
impression,

00:08:46.526 --> 00:08:48.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they ever --
-Everybody imitates

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
Richard Kind.
All of my friends --

00:08:49.395 --> 00:08:52.765
Dan Castellaneta, Hank Azaria --
and have done it

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:55.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's funny, funny,
funny, funny.

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can't do it.

00:08:56.369 --> 00:08:58.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just sound like this.
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:02.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, one time
I was at a poker game

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:05.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they asked --
you'll know how long ago.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a show called
"The Commish"

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.015 size:78% position:39% line:92%
with Michael Chiklis.

00:09:09.015 --> 00:09:11.951
I had a recurring role
on the show, so they say,

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:15.388
"Are you going to be playing
next week in the poker game?

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:17.990 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I said, "I can't.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.859 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm doing a 'Commish.'"

00:09:19.859 --> 00:09:22.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that has all of the vowels
that you need

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:24.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
to do Richard Kind.

00:09:24.564 --> 00:09:25.865 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So it's --

00:09:25.865 --> 00:09:28.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I can't do me,
but when I say,

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:31.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I can't.
I'm doing a 'Commish.'"

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:32.638 line:92%
And that's how I imitate me.

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:34.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
Otherwise,
I just sound like this.

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:38.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember, once,
you presenting an award

00:09:38.411 --> 00:09:41.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Writers Guild Award
-Mm-hmm.

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:45.117 line:92%
-and it was a very written bit

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:46.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I can't remember any
of the details,

00:09:46.586 --> 00:09:50.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
except that it did not go
particularly well.

00:09:50.222 --> 00:09:51.023 line:92%
And, when you finished it --

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:53.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is my
Richard Kind impression.

00:09:53.893 --> 00:09:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finished, sort of an awkward
silence. You just went --

00:09:58.364 --> 00:09:59.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Kind ]
Alright!

00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:00.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And that was --

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:06.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Clap ]
-So I recommend that.

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Kind ]
I'm doing a "Commish."

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is why
I don't do stand-up.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:10.643 line:92%
This is why I did improv.

00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:12.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Because you can't
blame anybody.

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:14.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
In improv, you go,
"Where the hell were you?

00:10:14.914 --> 00:10:17.316 size:84% position:42%
Why did you do that?!
Why did you say that?!"

00:10:17.316 --> 00:10:20.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you're standing up ther
alone and just go,

00:10:20.419 --> 00:10:22.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It's my fault."
-Yeah.

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:25.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
I felt like
maybe this was the rare case

00:10:25.691 --> 00:10:28.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the material did not ris
up to your level.

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:30.162 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-And the Writers Guild,

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:31.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
it was not that good.

00:10:31.864 --> 00:10:33.699 size:75% position:38%
I remember rewriting
a lot of their stuff

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:36.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not using their script
but then I also hosted

00:10:36.802 --> 00:10:41.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
the International Emmy Award
this year...

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:41.974 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, wow.

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:45.044 line:92%
-and I rewrote everything.

00:10:45.044 --> 00:10:47.446 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was a disaster.

00:10:47.446 --> 00:10:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:49.682 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was horrible!

00:10:49.682 --> 00:10:50.816 line:92%
But there was no audience.

00:10:50.816 --> 00:10:52.918
There was only the world.
It was all over the world,

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:56.722
except there was nobody ther
and you can't play the audience.

00:10:56.722 --> 00:10:59.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to ride the audience,
you know?

00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Horrible.
-You want to ride the audience

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:01.894 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
just like a ferret.

00:11:01.894 --> 00:11:03.829 line:92%
-Just like a parrot, baby!

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:04.964 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It's just like a ferret.

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, Richard, it's always such
a delight to talk to you.

00:11:08.134 --> 00:11:09.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please say hi
to your family, please.

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:10.936 line:92%
-I will, and you to yours.

00:11:10.936 --> 00:11:15.241
